    'ajuda.faqQ1': 'How do I connect the wearable to the dashboard?', 'ajuda.faqA1': 'Run "start_carewear.bat" (double-click, in the project folder) — it starts the bridge and opens the dashboard already connected, no terminal needed. Make sure the wearable is on and nearby. The connection appears in the top bar as soon as data starts arriving. Next to the indicator there is also a button to manually connect/disconnect the Bluetooth link to the device (useful to free it for firmware flashing or another tool), without needing to close the bridge.',
    'ajuda.faqQ6': 'How do I take a continuous HR/SpO₂ reading?', 'ajuda.faqA6': 'On the Vital signs view, use the "Continuous reading" button — it automatically resends the request while it\'s on, so you don\'t have to keep clicking "Measure now". Turn it off whenever you want to stop.',
    'ajuda.faqQ7': "How does the emergency alert work if the caregiver doesn't respond?", 'ajuda.faqA7': "In Settings, set your unavailability schedule (e.g. work hours) and an emergency contact. If an alert happens within those hours and you don't confirm in time, the system automatically notifies that contact — it never contacts real emergency services directly, that decision always stays with a person.",
    'ajuda.faqQ2': 'What happens if I lose the connection?', 'ajuda.faqA2': 'The dashboard switches to demo data and flags the status in the top bar. Live data returns automatically as soon as the connection is restored.',
    'ajuda.faqQ3': 'Is my data sent to the cloud?', 'ajuda.faqA3': 'No. In this prototype, all data is processed and stored locally on the device running the dashboard.',
    'ajuda.faqQ4': 'How do personalized thresholds work?', 'ajuda.faqA4': 'They are computed from the patient’s individual baseline instead of fixed values, so they adapt to their usual pattern. You can enable them in Settings.',
    'ajuda.faqQ5': 'How do I reset or erase the data?', 'ajuda.faqA5': 'In Settings, under the Danger zone, you can reset the device or permanently erase all local data.',
