    // --- ajuda FAQ Q8-Q16 (cobertura completa das funcionalidades) ---
    'ajuda.faqQ8': 'What is the difference between the two profiles (Patient/Family and Doctor/Technician)?',
    'ajuda.faqA8': 'Patient/Family sees their own routine, vital-sign, and medication data. Doctor/Technician manages multiple patients, sets clinical thresholds, reviews anomalies, and exports reports — different views, with different permissions.',
    'ajuda.faqQ9': 'How does the caregiver team and its permissions work?',
    'ajuda.faqA9': 'In Settings, the caregiver team lists who follows the patient, each with their own permissions to view alerts and edit notes. You can invite (simulated in this prototype) or remove someone at any time.',
    'ajuda.faqQ10': 'What does "Consent and data sharing" control?',
    'ajuda.faqA10': 'In Settings, it controls whether vital signs, routine, and alerts are shared with the clinical team — it only affects what the browser shows/exports, it is not enforced server-side (prototype).',
    'ajuda.faqQ11': 'How are anomalies detected in the clinical area?',
    'ajuda.faqA11': 'Two sources are combined: a duration rule (a block outside the expected range) and an LSTM Autoencoder that learns the usual pattern and flags deviations — see the limits for each in Duration limits.',
    'ajuda.faqQ12': 'What export formats exist and when should I use each one?',
    'ajuda.faqA12': 'FHIR (JSON, standard clinical format) and PDF (printable summary) export only what is visible in this session. CSV exports the real history stored in the bridge — use "Export everything" for the full history already stored, with no day limit.',
    'ajuda.faqQ13': 'Why does changing the NIF or address in the profile need approval?',
    'ajuda.faqA13': 'NIF and address are sensitive data — any change stays pending until the clinical team approves it, to prevent unverified changes to clinically-used data.',
    'ajuda.faqQ14': 'How do medication reminders and adherence analysis work?',
    'ajuda.faqA14': 'The browser notifies you when it is time to take a medication (±30 min window); marking it as taken updates adherence. The adherence analysis uses those real clicks (not the sample data in the 6-day history) to suggest adjustments.',
    'ajuda.faqQ15': 'What does "simulated data" mean on some charts?',
    'ajuda.faqA15': 'Several charts (routine, 7-day trend, weekly heatmap) still use sample data, clearly marked "simulated". Live vital signs (HR/SpO₂/steps) already use real data when the bridge is connected.',
    'ajuda.faqQ16': 'How do I change the language or theme (light/dark)?',
    'ajuda.faqA16': 'The language selector is in the top bar; the light/dark theme button is right next to it — your choice is saved in this browser.',
    'ajuda.faqQ17': 'How does the caregiver\'s activity correction work?',
    'ajuda.faqA17': 'When you correct the activity the AI classified, your correction becomes the panel\'s main line for 30 minutes (marked "confirmed by caregiver"), with the AI\'s classification shown as a secondary note. After 30 minutes, the AI classification takes the lead again. The correction is stored for a possible later re-evaluation of the classifier, but it does not retrain it in real time.',
